Relevant columns and how they will be used  
`bigquery-public-data.covid19_jhu_csse.summary`  
• `country_region`: country filter (US, France, China, Italy, Spain, Germany, Iran)  
• `date`: restrict to the snapshot “2020‑04‑20”  
• `confirmed`: will be summed per country to obtain total cases on that day

`bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`  
• `country_name`: same country filter as above (be aware that the World‑Bank spelling for the U.S. is `United States`)  
• `indicator_code`: population rows are identified by `SP.POP.TOTL` (“Population, total”)  
• `year`: restrict to 2020  
• `value`: 2020 population value; will be summed per country (for most countries there is only one row)  

Conditions that will be used  
• `WHERE date = '2020-04-20'` on the JHU table  
• `WHERE indicator_code = 'SP.POP.TOTL' AND year = 2020` on the World‑Bank table  
• `WHERE country_region IN (…)` or `country_name IN (…)` for the seven target countries  

Below are 10 progressively richer BigQuery SQL statements (each limited to 20 rows) that explore the data and finally produce the requested figures.

```sql
-- 1) Inspect available dates in the JHU summary table
SELECT DISTINCT date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_jhu_csse.summary`
ORDER BY date
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Quick look at the April‑20‑2020 snapshot for all records
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_jhu_csse.summary`
WHERE date = '2020-04-20'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Confirmed cases on 2020-04-20 for the seven target countries (no aggregation yet)
SELECT country_region, province_state, confirmed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_jhu_csse.summary`
WHERE date = '2020-04-20'
  AND country_region IN ('US','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Aggregate confirmed cases for the seven countries on 2020-04-20
SELECT country_region,
       SUM(confirmed) AS total_confirmed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_jhu_csse.summary`
WHERE date = '2020-04-20'
  AND country_region IN ('US','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran')
GROUP BY country_region
ORDER BY total_confirmed DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Inspect indicator codes that look like population counts
SELECT DISTINCT indicator_code
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
WHERE LOWER(indicator_name) LIKE '%population%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Pull 2020 total‑population rows for the seven countries
SELECT country_name,
       value AS population_2020
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
WHERE indicator_code = 'SP.POP.TOTL'
  AND year = 2020
  AND country_name IN ('United States','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran, Islamic Rep.')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Aggregate population values in case a country has multiple sub‑rows (usually it doesn’t)
SELECT country_name,
       SUM(value) AS population_2020
FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
WHERE indicator_code = 'SP.POP.TOTL'
  AND year = 2020
  AND country_name IN ('United States','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran, Islamic Rep.')
GROUP BY country_name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Join confirmed cases with population to compute cases per 100,000 people
WITH cases AS (
  SELECT country_region,
         SUM(confirmed) AS total_confirmed
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_jhu_csse.summary`
  WHERE date = '2020-04-20'
    AND country_region IN ('US','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran')
  GROUP BY country_region
),
pop AS (
  SELECT country_name,
         SUM(value) AS population_2020
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
  WHERE indicator_code = 'SP.POP.TOTL'
    AND year = 2020
    AND country_name IN ('United States','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran, Islamic Rep.')
  GROUP BY country_name
)
SELECT
  c.country_region AS country,
  c.total_confirmed,
  p.population_2020,
  ROUND(c.total_confirmed * 100000.0 / p.population_2020, 2) AS cases_per_100k
FROM cases AS c
JOIN pop  AS p
  ON ( (c.country_region = 'US'      AND p.country_name = 'United States') OR
       (c.country_region = p.country_name) OR
       (c.country_region = 'Iran'    AND p.country_name = 'Iran, Islamic Rep.') )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Same as #8 but sorting by cases per 100k (final answer query)
WITH cases AS (
  SELECT country_region,
         SUM(confirmed) AS total_confirmed
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_jhu_csse.summary`
  WHERE date = '2020-04-20'
    AND country_region IN ('US','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran')
  GROUP BY country_region
),
pop AS (
  SELECT country_name,
         SUM(value) AS population_2020
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
  WHERE indicator_code = 'SP.POP.TOTL'
    AND year = 2020
    AND country_name IN ('United States','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran, Islamic Rep.')
  GROUP BY country_name
)
SELECT
  c.country_region AS country,
  c.total_confirmed,
  p.population_2020,
  ROUND(c.total_confirmed * 100000.0 / p.population_2020, 2) AS cases_per_100k
FROM cases AS c
JOIN pop  AS p
  ON ( (c.country_region = 'US'      AND p.country_name = 'United States') OR
       (c.country_region = p.country_name) OR
       (c.country_region = 'Iran'    AND p.country_name = 'Iran, Islamic Rep.') )
ORDER BY cases_per_100k DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Advanced variant: use WINDOW functions to put each metric into rank order
WITH cases AS (
  SELECT country_region,
         SUM(confirmed) AS total_confirmed
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_jhu_csse.summary`
  WHERE date = '2020-04-20'
    AND country_region IN ('US','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran')
  GROUP BY country_region
),
pop AS (
  SELECT country_name,
         SUM(value) AS population_2020
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.world_bank_health_population.health_nutrition_population`
  WHERE indicator_code = 'SP.POP.TOTL'
    AND year = 2020
    AND country_name IN ('United States','France','China','Italy','Spain','Germany','Iran, Islamic Rep.')
  GROUP BY country_name
),
joined AS (
  SELECT
    c.country_region AS country,
    c.total_confirmed,
    p.population_2020,
    ROUND(c.total_confirmed * 100000.0 / p.population_2020, 2) AS cases_per_100k
  FROM cases AS c
  JOIN pop  AS p
    ON ( (c.country_region = 'US'      AND p.country_name = 'United States') OR
         (c.country_region = p.country_name) OR
         (c.country_region = 'Iran'    AND p.country_name = 'Iran, Islamic Rep.') )
)
SELECT *,
       RANK() OVER (ORDER BY total_confirmed DESC)     AS rank_total_cases,
       RANK() OVER (ORDER BY cases_per_100k DESC)      AS rank_per_100k
FROM joined
LIMIT 20;
```

These queries allow you to verify dates, examine raw records, isolate the required population rows, and finally produce the total confirmed cases and the number of cases per 100,000 inhabitants for the United States, France, China, Italy, Spain, Germany, and Iran as of 20 April 2020.
